{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01306",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.06,
      "end_seconds": 9.22,
      "duration_seconds": 8.16,
      "text": "let me think, um, doctor? Hello, I hope this is the right time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.82,
      "end_seconds": 15.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 17.63,
      "end_seconds": 30.99,
      "duration_seconds": 13.36,
      "text": "Good morning, um, doctor. I came along to help out. It's blood on the toilet paper, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.37,
      "end_seconds": 38.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.19,
      "end_seconds": 49.18,
      "duration_seconds": 9.99,
      "text": "I'm not sure when it began, to be honest some weeks ago, but I can't say how many"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.75,
      "end_seconds": 53.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Is anything making it worse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.22,
      "end_seconds": 69.23,
      "duration_seconds": 14.01,
      "text": "Well, you know, I notice it more with hard stools. Pain when I pass stool was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.14,
      "end_seconds": 75.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Did you get weight loss or black stools?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.84,
      "end_seconds": 78.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.07,
      "end_seconds": 88.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "Did you get fever, change in bowel habit or family history of bowel cancer?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.68,
      "end_seconds": 97.28,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "No, no fever, change in bowel habit or family history of bowel cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.31,
      "end_seconds": 100.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.82,
      "end_seconds": 104.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "no, my breathing's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.38,
      "end_seconds": 108.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Have you been to to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.57,
      "end_seconds": 114.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "I had my tonsils removed as a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.82,
      "end_seconds": 118.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.92,
      "end_seconds": 121.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "I've got low haemoglobin"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.04,
      "end_seconds": 128.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Ah. Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.26,
      "end_seconds": 148.0,
      "duration_seconds": 14.74,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. No, I share a house with my brother. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.52,
      "end_seconds": 170.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.05,
      "end_seconds": 173.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "my mother had a stroke"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.76,
      "end_seconds": 177.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "what's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 177.89,
      "end_seconds": 183.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "She takes iron tablets, once a day for my blood count."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.58,
      "end_seconds": 196.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.05,
      "end_seconds": 207.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "That's it, just a a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.99,
      "end_seconds": 232.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 97 percent, pulse 76, BP is 109 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.79,
      "end_seconds": 241.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.88,
      "end_seconds": 244.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "that's fine, I'll explain it soon"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.56,
      "end_seconds": 249.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 250.8,
      "end_seconds": 251.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.5,
      "end_seconds": 256.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.23,
      "end_seconds": 275.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "There's a small external pile at the edge, and I don't see any fissure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.94,
      "end_seconds": 278.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.99,
      "end_seconds": 291.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Tummy is soft and non-tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.37,
      "end_seconds": 297.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "good, you can sit up again"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.48,
      "end_seconds": 321.83,
      "duration_seconds": 15.35,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, I don't have a clear answer today: haemorrhoids is possible, and so is something higher up in the bowel that we shouldn't miss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.71,
      "end_seconds": 324.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.13,
      "end_seconds": 364.89,
      "duration_seconds": 36.76,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now haemorrhoids is my leading thought, not anything worse. We should do blood tests for rectal bleeding. I think a colonoscopy makes sense here, for rectal bleeding. Let's use a soothing cream, twice a day, for one week. That should help with haemorrhoids. You'll be taking lactulose, 15 ml, at night, for two weeks. It's for constipation. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.55,
      "end_seconds": 388.87,
      "duration_seconds": 20.32,
      "text": "soak in a warm bath for ten minutes after you pass stool, and don't strain. Let's get you seen by a colorectal surgeon, I'll arrange the letter. Come back in three weeks. Okay, is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 390.78,
      "end_seconds": 394.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "I, I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}